<?xml version="1.0"?>
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <move element="ves.quotation" destination="theme.headers"/>
        <!--
            The cross-sell carousel USED to be injected into `minicart.addons`
            here. It has been removed, on measurement rather than taste.

            The block sets $_maxItemCount = 8 (core uses 4) and the theme's rail
            grid is a fixed four columns, so inside the 340px dropdown it laid
            out two rows of eight cards at 64px wide: names truncated mid-word,
            prices sliced through the glyph, and the second row below the fold of
            a 1000px viewport. It also rendered in the header on EVERY page of
            the site, not just the cart.

            Nothing is lost on /cart — that page's "More Choices:" is a
            DIFFERENT block (core's `checkout.cart.crosssell`, rendered by
            Magento_Catalog::product/list/items.phtml, which the theme now
            overrides). The merchandising slot survives where it has room to work.

            To restore it, re-add the block below and give it
            `grid-template-columns: 1fr` scoped to `.block-minicart` plus a real
            item cap — `products_count` is not honoured by this block.
        -->

        <referenceBlock name="quotes_links" remove="true" />
    </body>
</page>